<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Gabriel Villagrán, his engineering work, learning path, and the people who helped shape it.">
  <header class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">About Gabriel</span><h1>Curiosity, applied.</h1><p>I’m a software engineer from Mexico. I enjoy solving practical problems, explaining technical ideas clearly, and learning from the people I work with.</p></header>
  <div class="content-layout">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>My experience spans iOS engineering, backend integrations, web interfaces, and industrial systems. I’ve built Swift experiences for cart and checkout, connected mobile and web clients to Laravel APIs, and worked on SCADA monitoring and SQL-backed reporting. I care about dependable software and clear collaboration across teams.</p>
      <p>This site also holds an archive of writing from LaunchX, a Microsoft-supported learning program I joined in 2022. I’ve revised those posts for clarity and technical accuracy while keeping their original publication dates. They show where I started and how my thinking has developed.</p>
      <h2>People who helped me grow</h2>
      <p>I’m grateful to the mentors and educators who shared their time and perspective during my studies and early projects: Dr. Pedro David Arjona Villicaña, Dr. José Ignacio Núñez Varela, Fernanda Ochoa, Rodrigo Martínez, and Carlo Gilmar. Their guidance helped me build the habit of asking better questions, practicing consistently, and sharing what I learn.</p>
      <p>Outside software, I enjoy music, games, and time with family and friends.</p>
      <div class="quote-card"><blockquote>“Don’t let the theory stop you from reaching your goal.”</blockquote><p>A reminder I kept from my early learning journey: understand the ideas, then put them to work.</p></div>
    </div>
